From: Alex Kiernan <alex.kiernan@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fastboot: include <string.h> for memcpy()

fastboot_driver_interface.h calls memcpy() without including <string.h>; it
builds on Android because the libc++ headers pull it in transitively, but
not with GCC and libstdc++:

  fastboot_driver_interface.h:89:21: error: 'memcpy' was not declared in this scope

Upstream-Status: Pending

AI-Generated: Claude Opus 5.5 (Claude Code)
Signed-off-by: Alex Kiernan <alex.kiernan@gmail.com>
---
--- a/system/core/fastboot/fastboot_driver_interface.h
+++ b/system/core/fastboot/fastboot_driver_interface.h
@@ -15,6 +15,8 @@
 //
 #pragma once
 
+#include <string.h>
+
 #include <functional>
 #include <string>
 #include <vector>
